# Model & Experiment Rules

All models and training are Python/PyTorch. See `docs/BASELINE_PROTOCOL.md` +
`docs/SESSION_DRIFT_ANALYSIS.md` (current mainline) and `docs/ROADMAP.md` /
`docs/MODEL_PLAN.md` / `docs/EXPERIMENT_PROTOCOL.md` (future full CAP-EEGNet).

## CURRENT MAINLINE: fair within/cross-session comparison (do not weaken)

- **One protocol, one data filter, one metric set for ALL models.** Baselines
  (EEGNet/DeepConvNet/FBCNet) and CAP-EEGNet MUST use the same `src/training/trainer.py`,
  the same `src/evaluation/session_protocols.py`, the same `status=ok` filter, and the
  same metrics. Never give one model an advantage (different epochs, data, or eval).
- **No data leakage**, enforced in `session_protocols.py`:
  - within-session: StratifiedKFold; test fold disjoint from train; the early-stopping
    val slice is carved from train only.
  - cross-session: train and test are DIFFERENT sessions (directed pairs, same subject).
  - never mix within (no drift) and cross (drift); the derivatives `.mat` is never used.
- All four models share the forward contract `{"logits", "features", "confidence"}`
  (confidence is `None` for baselines, a learned scalar for CAP-EEGNet v1).
- Metrics: Accuracy, Balanced Accuracy, Macro-F1, AUC, NLL, Brier, ECE; report
  cross-session drop and relative drop. Smoke-test (subjects 1,2) before any full run.
- **CAP-EEGNet is v1** (encoder + classifier + learned confidence head). Prototype,
  multi-source confidence, adapter, domain alignment, neural subagents, and online update
  are future work and must raise `NotImplementedError` if enabled — never silently ship
  v1 as the full method.
- LOSO, 41/10 cross-subject pretraining, fine-tuning, and online learning are FUTURE WORK
  right now (see `docs/EXPERIMENT_PROTOCOL.md`); do not run them in the current mainline.

